DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The iissppuunncctt() and iissppuunncctt__ll() functions test for any printing character
     except for space (‘ ’) or a character for which isalnum(3) or
     isalnum_l(3) is true.  The value of the argument must be representable as
     an _u_n_s_i_g_n_e_d _c_h_a_r or the value of EOF.

     In the ASCII character set, this includes the following characters (with
     their numeric values shown in octal):

     041 ``!''     042 ``"''     043 ``#''     044 ``$''     045 ``%''
     046 ``&''     047 ``'''     050 ``(''     051 ``)''     052 ``*''
     053 ``+''     054 ``,''     055 ``-''     056 ``.''     057 ``/''
     072 ``:''     073 ``;''     074 ``<''     075 ``=''     076 ``>''
     077 ``?''     100 ``@''     133 ``[''     134 ``\''     135 ``]''
     136 ``^''     137 ``_''     140 ```''     173 ``{''     174 ``|''
     175 ``}''     176 ``~''

     The iissppuunncctt__ll() function takes an explicit locale argument, whereas the
     iissppuunncctt() function uses the current global or per-thread locale.

